# Root-level safety net — backend/ and frontend/ each have their own .gitignore for their
# specifics; this covers anything created at the repo root so a future root-level .env,
# key, or dump isn't tracked by default (SecurityIssues.md I-2).

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!*/.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks

*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql.gz

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Terraform (Roadmap_Scaling.md B2) — state can contain resource attributes that are
# effectively secrets (RDS/ElastiCache endpoints, etc.), and .tfvars often carries
# environment-specific values not meant for git. Remote state lives in S3; nothing
# Terraform-related belongs in this repo's history.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Claude Code personal/session-local settings (permission rules etc.) — not shared with
# the team via the committed project settings.json.
.claude/settings.local.json
